<title>USA: Cargo plane had four crew on board, FAA says.</title>
<headline>Cargo plane had four crew on board, FAA says.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were four crew members on board the Fine AIR DC-8 cargo plane that crashed on take-off from Miami International Airport, the Federal Aviation Administration said Thursday.</p>
<p>FAA spokesman Eliot Brenner said preliminary information was that the plane came down about a mile from the end of the runway at 12:34 p.m. EDT.  </p>
<p>&quot;The preliminary information we have now is that the aircraft was operated by Fine AIR as flight 101,&quot; Brenner said.</p>
<p>&quot;The aircraft is a DC-8 cargo flight and we understand there were four persons on board.&quot;</p>
